<p class="eyebrow">Fortress revival &middot; coordinator skill &middot; skill drafts &middot; version 22 &middot; 7 November 2026</p>
<h1>Your held rules, version 22</h1>
<p class="standfirst">Version 22. Two landed changes that you have not read, and one draft that waits for your yes. Item 30, a new rule: a batch record takes every well-defined piece of work that moves the project forward, unless it would put the merge at risk, as you said this morning. Item 31, a rule whose meaning changed: while a batch runs, the coordinator and the skill writer may commit the skills, the boot note and the held list in the main tree until every rung&rsquo;s worker has started, and nothing changes there from then until the batch&rsquo;s push. Draft 32: before every task of the skill writer that has its own cold read, the coordinator reads the held list and adds every point that waits for the writer.</p>
</header>

