<section id="s2" class="part">
<h2>Proposed changes</h2>
<p>One draft waits for your yes to its exact words: draft 32. It shows its new text whole, with the added words underlined, and its current text collapsed.</p>

<section id="d32" class="part item">
<h3><span class="num">Draft 32 &middot; SKILL.md, &ldquo;The record: what goes where&rdquo;, the bullet on the held list, line 233</span>The held list read before every writer task with its own cold read</h3>
<div class="change solo"><div><span class="side">Proposed text, not landed; underlined, the words that come in. In the skill's words, &ldquo;you&rdquo; is the coordinator.</span>
<ul><li>Put on the held list each rule that the curator states about your work, and each change to how you work that you and the curator agree in conversation. Have the skill writer (<code>references/skill-rewrite.md</code>) put it into its skill at the next opportunity, as &ldquo;The curator&rsquo;s role and decisions&rdquo; says. <span class="add">That opportunity is the next task that you give the writer that has its own cold read, not a task that only fixes a cold read&rsquo;s flags. Before you give that task, read the held list, and add to the task each point that names the skill writer. Leave out a point of a reading that the curator has not said is done, and a point for <code>fortress-repo</code> while the record-landing workflow runs.</span> The curator&rsquo;s rule in conversation is not a yes to the skill&rsquo;s wording. Keep it on the held list until <span class="add">its skill holds it</span>. If a compaction comes <span class="add">before that</span>, quote the held rule into the boot note, so that the session after the boot works that way.</li></ul>
</div></div>
<details class="prior"><summary>Current text (tap to open)</summary><div>
<ul><li>Put on the held list each rule that the curator states about your work, and each change to how you work that you and the curator agree in conversation. Have the skill writer (<code>references/skill-rewrite.md</code>) put it into its skill at the next opportunity, as &ldquo;The curator&rsquo;s role and decisions&rdquo; says. The curator&rsquo;s rule in conversation is not a yes to the skill&rsquo;s wording. Keep it on the held list until <span class="cut">then</span>. If a compaction comes <span class="cut">first</span>, quote the held rule into the boot note, so that the session after the boot works that way.</li></ul>
</div></details>
<div class="note"><p><strong>What it changes.</strong> &ldquo;At the next opportunity&rdquo; now names a moment: the next task that the coordinator gives the skill writer that has its own cold read. A task that only fixes a cold read&rsquo;s flags does not count, since it gets no cold read of its own. Before that task, the coordinator reads the held list and adds to the task every point for the skill writer. It leaves out the points of a reading that you have not yet said is done, since the reading keeps its points until its end. It also leaves out a point for <code>fortress-repo</code> while the record-landing workflow runs, since that workflow changes <code>fortress-repo</code> then. &ldquo;Until then&rdquo; and &ldquo;first&rdquo; now name the moment when the skill holds the point.</p>
<p><strong>Why.</strong> Before the compaction, the coordinator gave the skill writer your rule of 05:5x UTC, that the first batch landing after a light boot reads FACTS and POSITIONS whole. It left your rule of 05:2x UTC on what a batch takes on the held list, because no rule made it read the held list first. That rule has since landed, as item 30. Between 07:10 and 07:20 UTC you asked that &ldquo;a curator triggered update of skills should write a proposal of all skill updates from the held list as well&rdquo;.</p>
<p>The draft is wider than your words, and that part is the coordinator&rsquo;s proposal. It sweeps the held list before every task of the skill writer that has its own cold read, not only before one that you start, since every such task is a chance to bring a held rule into its skill, and the cost is small. It waits for your yes because it touches how the points of the held list reach the skills.</p></div>
</section>

